op all charges against Edward Snowden.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/34"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":6,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr275-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-27","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs."},"number":"HR 275","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Special Interest Alien Reporting Act of 2024 [ sic ] This bill requires the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to report every month on non-U.S. nationals ( aliens under federal law) who attempt to unlawfully enter the United States and who potentially pose a national security risk. DHS must report on (1) the number of individuals, (2) the nationalities or countries of last residence of these...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Special Interest Alien Reporting Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/275"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":17,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr276-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-12","text":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 73."},"number":"HR 276","policyArea":"Public Lands and Natural Resources","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Gulf of America Act of 2025 This bill renames the Gulf of Mexico as the Gulf of America and directs federal agencies to update their documents and maps to incorporate the new name.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Gulf of America Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/276"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr277-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the Committee on the Judiciary, and in addition to the Committee on Intelligence (Permanent Select), for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"number":"HR 277","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Matthew Lawrence Perna Act of 2025 This bill limits certain actions by the federal government related to the criminal prosecution and sentencing of individuals who are charged with a political protest offense. A political protest offense is a federal criminal offense that arises out of protest activities and is not a crime of violence. The bill also makes other changes that apply more broadly to...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Matthew Lawrence Perna Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/277"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":11,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres24-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HRES 24","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This resolution expunges the December 18, 2019, impeachment of President Trump.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Expunging the December 18, 2019, impeachment of President Donald John Trump.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/24"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":11,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres25-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HRES 25","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This resolution expunges the January 13, 2021, impeachment of President Trump.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Expunging the January 13, 2021, impeachment of President Donald John Trump.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/25"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":5,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres26-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HRES 26","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This resolution deems certain conduct of members of antifa as domestic terrorism and designates antifa as a domestic terrorist organization. The resolution calls on the Department of Justice to (1) prosecute crimes of domestic terrorism by antifa, and (2) use all available tools and resources to combat the spread of such terrorism by antifa.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Deeming certain conduct of members of Antifa as domestic terrorism and designating Antifa as a domestic terrorist organization.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/26"}],"state":"GA","topCrossPartyCollaborators":[{"bioguideId":"M001137","caucus":"D","count":1,"name":"Gregory W. Meeks"},{"bioguideId":"K000389","caucus":"D","count":1,"name":"Ro Khanna"},{"bioguideId":"C001110","caucus":"D","count":1,"name":"J. Luis Correa"}]}
